failure_location.quote:
The amplification factor $G$ satisfying
\begin{equation}
G(\infty)=0,
\label{G_infty}
\end{equation}
if and only if
\begin{equation}
C+D=0,
\label{L_stable_Condition}
\end{equation}

If and only if
\begin{equation}
C\geq0 \quad \text{or}\quad C<-\frac{1}{39},
\end{equation}
we have
\begin{equation}
{\textnormal{Re}}(z)>0,
\end{equation}
i.e., all roots of the equation \eqref{equation_C}  lie in the right half-plane,
in another words, the amplification factor $G(z)$ is analytic in $\textnormal{Re}(z)\leq 0$.

achieves A-stability under the condition
\begin{equation}
D=-C,
\end{equation}
with the parameter $C$ confined to the interval
\begin{equation}
C \in [0.018824, 0.045589],
\label{C_domain}
\end{equation}
